# The container's local environment file.
#
# **.env.example is tracked and .env is not**, and it was not ignored either,
# so on any host that had followed the container instructions it sat untracked
# forever. Go marks a build "+dirty" for untracked files as well as modified
# ones, so every image built there reported
# `0.1.121 (v0.1.94-...-38282c7ec6b5+dirty)` — and a flag that is always on
# carries no information. It exists to say "this binary contains changes that
# are not in the commit", which is exactly what an operator needs to know and
# now could not learn.
deploy/docker/.env

# The Zello connector's file, which the console's Zello page generates and an
# operator saves beside docker-compose.zello.yml. Ignored for the reason .env
# is: an untracked file marks every build from that checkout +dirty.
deploy/docker/qsp-zello.json
